WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.125 --> 00:00:02.335
My name is David Clark
 and I'm a neuroscientist.

00:00:02.335 --> 00:00:05.922
The central question in neuroscience is
 how does the brain work?

00:00:05.922 --> 00:00:08.425
I study vision, and what I really love
 doing is designing visual stimuli

00:00:08.425 --> 00:00:13.722
that allow us to test very specific
 hypotheses about how the brain works.

00:00:13.722 --> 00:00:18.018
That's sort of one of the joys, I think,
 in lab, is doing that sort of design work.

00:00:18.018 --> 00:00:20.937
We study this in the fruit fly Drosophila.

00:00:20.937 --> 00:00:23.064
The mathematical processing
 that's happening in our brain

00:00:23.064 --> 00:00:26.317
and in the fly's
 brain is really quite similar.

00:00:26.317 --> 00:00:29.821
We have designed virtual reality
 devices for flies.

00:00:29.821 --> 00:00:33.658
These are very small virtual reality
 devices that have screens on three sides.

00:00:33.658 --> 00:00:36.911
And then we pin the fly in place
 and suspend it over a little ball.

00:00:36.911 --> 00:00:39.998
So it walks on this treadmill
 and then we can monitor how the fly

00:00:39.998 --> 00:00:43.251
is walking in response
 to various visual stimuli.

00:00:43.251 --> 00:00:44.919
What's cool about Drosophila 

00:00:44.919 --> 00:00:49.340
is that we can actually use genetics
 to manipulate their brain.

00:00:49.340 --> 00:00:51.092
We can turn different parts of the brain on or off 

00:00:51.092 --> 00:00:55.138
to see how those affect the fly's behavior.

00:00:55.138 --> 00:00:57.599
The hope here is
 that we're studying flies,

00:00:57.599 --> 00:01:02.604
but we're also going to learn principles
 that will apply to humans and other animals. 

00:01:02.604 --> 00:01:05.523
What's fun to be able to do is be able to

00:01:05.523 --> 00:01:09.027
connect individual proteins in single cells,

00:01:09.027 --> 00:01:13.281
move from single cells to collections of connected cells,

00:01:13.281 --> 00:01:15.325
and then to whole regions of the brain,

00:01:15.325 --> 00:01:17.452
and then to behavior.

00:01:18.244 --> 00:01:22.707
That ability to make these connections
 between different levels of understanding

00:01:22.707 --> 00:01:27.003
is what's really powerful in neuroscience
 and what's really exciting right now.

